00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.240
Christmas is celebrated in many cultures
around the world in many different ways.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:12.640
But there is one tradition common
to all of them, giving gifts.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.080
Why is that?

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.320
What's the connection
between gifts and Christmas.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:24.120
It started with the gifts God gave to all
of us, the universe, galaxies, stars,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:29.360
animals, the Earth we live on,
the very gift of life.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.800
These are all gifts
given by a God who loves us,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.280
knows us, and wants us to know him.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.480
But something has gone wrong.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.520
We have turned away from the one
who gave us these gifts.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.600
We have treated them
with carelessness and neglect.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.800
We've even convinced ourselves they
weren't gifts at all, that they

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.320
just happened and they mean nothing.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.720
Thus, we have become alienated
from our maker and from one another.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.760
So what does all this
have to do with Christmas?

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.480
2000 years ago,
a baby was born in an insignificant

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.680
town ruled by a powerful empire.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.600
Christmas is the celebration of his birth.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.240
Why was he so special that we
now celebrate his birth today?

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.800
We celebrate because even though we have
turned our back on him,

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.840
God decided to give us the best
gift of all, the gift of himself.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.920
He came down to Earth as a human being
to live and die and rise again,

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.320
all to show us that he knows us and loves
us and gives each one of us

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.800
the opportunity to know him.

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.480
His name is Jesus.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:40.240
And today, Jesus wants to give each one
of us a new gift,

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.880
the gift of life and a fresh start,
the gift of forgiveness and a personal

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:51.560
relationship with our maker,
and the promise of eternal life.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.880
Jesus is the gift we
celebrate at Christmas.

